## Scope and assets

Protected assets include tenant configuration, management groups, subscriptions,
Terraform state, workflow definitions, federated identities, policy
assignments, diagnostic data, network boundaries, and production workloads.

## Trust boundaries

1. Contributor workstation → GitHub pull request.
2. GitHub Actions → Entra workload identity federation.
#{{IF computed.backendIsHcp}}
3. GitHub Actions → HCP Terraform.
4. HCP Terraform → Azure dynamic provider credentials.
#{{ELSE}}
3. GitHub Actions → Azure Storage state backend using Entra ID.
#{{ENDIF}}
5. Platform subscriptions → workload subscriptions.
6. Hub network → spokes and private endpoints.
7. Azure control plane → diagnostic destinations.

## Principal threats and controls

| Threat | Preventive controls | Detective/recovery controls |
|---|---|---|
| Untrusted PR obtains write token | Separate plan/apply apps; exact OIDC subjects; no `pull_request_target` | OIDC verification workflow; Entra sign-in logs |
| Workflow supply-chain compromise | Full-SHA action pins; locked root permissions | Action-pinning and security checks |
| Unauthorized production apply | Protected environment; approval chain; trusted default-branch checkout | Workflow audit trail and activity logs |
| Terraform state disclosure or corruption | Isolated layer state; Entra auth; least privilege | State versioning, locking, recovery procedure |
| Out-of-band Azure changes | IaC-only operating model and policy | Scheduled drift detection and Azure Activity Log |
| Network data exfiltration | Hub-spoke boundaries, firewall, private endpoints, public-access policy | NSG flow logs, diagnostics, threat intelligence |
| Privilege persistence | PIM-eligible model and separate identities | Access reviews, role-assignment inventory |
| Destructive change | Plan inspection and destructive-apply refusal | Backup, state recovery, DR runbook |

## Identity invariants

- Plan subject: `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.oidcSubjectPullRequest}}`.
- Apply subjects are environment-bound; wildcard subjects are forbidden.
- Plan identity is read-only.
- Apply identity is unavailable to pull-request jobs.
- Bootstrap operator access is interactive and MFA-protected.

See [identity-trust-matrix.md](identity-trust-matrix.md) for the generated
subject inventory.

